msgstr "%(site)s Sinadura egiaztatzea"

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "%(site)s chat supports [markdown formatting](/help/formatting)."
msgstr "%(site)s berriketak onartzen du [markdown formatua](/help/formatting)."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "%(site)s chooses to implement only minimal rules. Almost all First-Amendment-protected speech is permitted on %(site)s."
msgstr "%(site)sk arau minimoak ezartzea aukeratzen du. Lehen aho batez babesturiko ia hitz guztiak onartzen dira %(site)s(e)n."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "%(site)s is an open-source platform for online communities, free of censorship and moderator abuse by design."
msgstr "%(site)s lineako komunitateentzako kode irekiko plataforma da, zentsurarik eta moderatzaileen erabilerarik gabe."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "%(site)s is an open-source platform that powers independent online communities."
msgstr "%(site)s iturburu irekiko plataforma bat da, lineako komunitate independenteak boteretzen dituena."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "%(site)s is an open-source web app that lets you enjoy online communities focused around topics you love, without censorship and moderator abuse."
msgstr "%(site)s kode irekiko web aplikazio bat da, maite dituzun gaiei buruzko online komunitateez gozatzeko aukera ematen duena, zentsurarik eta moderatzaileen gehiegikeriarik gabe."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "%(site)s is broken into numerous smaller messaging and commenting boards focused around a variety of topics. These boards are called \"Guilds\". Guild names always start with a `+` symbol, and are usually (though not always) named after their topic of interest. For example, [+news](/+news) is a Guild focused on sharing and discussion of news and current events."
msgstr "%(site)s hainbat mezu txikiagotan banatzen da eta hainbat gairi buruzko iruzkinak egiten ditu. Taula horiei \"Guilds\" esaten zaie. Guild izenak beti `+` batekin hasten dira Ikurrak dira, eta normalean (baina ez beti) interes-gaiaren izena dute. Adibidez, [+news](/+news) Guild bat da, berriak eta uneko gertaerak partekatzeko eta eztabaidatzeko."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "%(site)s titles are text-based, cosmetic achievements that can be displayed next to your username across the %(site)s platform. Titles may be earned through various activities on %(site)s: earning rep, inviting friends, helping staff, and more."
msgstr "%(site)s izenburuak testuetan oinarritutakoak dira, kosmetika lorpenak, zure erabiltzaile-izenaren ondoan %(site)s plataforman zehar bistaratu daitezkeenak. Tituluak %(site)s(e)ko hainbat jardueraren bidez lor daitezke: ospea irabaztea, lagunak gonbidatzea, langileei laguntzea eta gehiago."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "%(site)s: Awesome Online Communities, Without Censorship"
msgstr "%(site)s: lineako komunitate zoragarriak, zentsurarik gabe"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "**Every automated post carries the robot mark**, people who turn on **Hide bot content** don't see them, and your profile says **Some posts are automated**. Your own posts carry no mark."
msgstr "** Postu automatiko bakoitzak robotaren marka darama**, **Bota-eduki ezkutuak** ez dituzte ikusten, eta zure profilek dio **mezu batzuk automatizatuta daudela**. Zure mezuek ez dute markarik."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "**Your feeds can't get your account suspended.** When a feed repeats itself, that item simply isn't posted. Your own posts are judged on their own, as before."
msgstr "**Zure iturriak ezin du zure kontua eten.** Iturri bat errepikatzen denean, elementu hori ez da argitaratzen. Zure postuak beren kabuz epaitzen dira, lehen bezala."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "**Your own account** can post from feeds too, while you keep using it as yourself: see [below](#own-account)."
msgstr "**Zure kontua ere bidal daiteke iturburuetatik, zuk bezala erabiltzen duzun bitartean: ikusi [beh](#own-account)."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "**Your server only orders.** Every post it names goes through the same rules as any feed before it is shown: removed posts, private guilds, each viewer's word filter and blocks. A post a viewer may not see is simply left out."
msgstr "**Zure zerbitzariak aginduak bakarrik.** Izendatzen duen mezu bakoitzak edozein iturriren arau berberak ditu, aurretik erakutsiak izan aurretik: kendutako mezuak, ontzi pribatuak, ikustaile bakoitzaren hitz-iragazkia eta blokeak. Ikustaile batek ikusten ez duen posta itzali besterik ez dago."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Anonymous #3.</b> In one thread, everyone who is anonymous there has a number, given in the order they became anonymous there (when they posted or commented anonymously, or when a delete, \"Remove my name\" or closing their account made it so). It is the same number on a post and on that person's anonymous comments, a different one in every other thread, and it stays when an account is deleted. It tells people apart; it never says who they are."
msgstr "<b>Anonimoa #3.</b> Hari batean, anonimo guztiek zenbaki bat dute, anonimo bihurtu ziren ordenan (modu anonimoan argitaratu edo iruzkindu zutenean, edo ezabatzean, \"Kendu nire izena\" edo kontua ixtean). Postu bateko zenbaki bera da, eta pertsona horren iruzkin anonimoetan, beste bat beste edozein haritan, eta kontu bat ezabatzen denean gelditzen da. Jendeak bereizten ditu; ez du inoiz esaten nor diren."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Bans that cite what someone wrote.</b> When an admin bans or suspends an account they may cite the posts and comments that justify it, even ones written anonymously. Once a second admin agrees, the Log names the account for those items (the line about each one, and the ban's line), so anyone can check the ban was fair. The items stay anonymous everywhere else on the site, nothing is named without that second admin, and reversing the ban takes the name back out."
msgstr "<b>Norbaitek idatzitakoa debekatzen du.</b> Kontu bat debekatu edo esekitzen duenean, hura justifikatzen duten mezuak eta iruzkinak aipa ditzakete, baita modu anonimoan idatzitakoak ere. Bigarren administratzaile bat ados jartzen denean, egunkariek elementu horien kontua izendatzen dute (lerro bakoitza eta debekuaren lerroa), eta, beraz, edonork ikus dezake debekua bidezkoa dela. Elementuak anonimoak dira guneko beste leku guztietan, ez da ezer izendatzen bigarren administratzaile hori gabe, eta debekuari uko egiteak izena atzera botatzen du."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Comments under a deleted post stay.</b> They are read under the post in the Log, where the post is Anonymous. The comments you wrote under your own post become Anonymous with it. A comment its own author deletes is shown as Anonymous there too."
msgstr "<b>Iruzkinak ezabatutako egonaldi baten azpian.</b> Egunkariko postaren azpian irakurtzen dira, non posta anonimoa den. Zure postaren azpian idatzi dituzun iruzkinak anonimo bihurtzen dira. Bere egilearen ezabapenak anonimo gisa ere erakusten dira."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Delete it.</b> It leaves the site. What it said (the title, the link and the text) stays in the Log as <b>Anonymous</b>: no name, no profile and no link, and a link in it is shown as plain text. Anyone can read it there, under the same word filter, sensitive-content and Child-level rules as any member's words. It is how a record of the site stays honest: like Wikipedia, every contribution remains."
msgstr "<b>Ezabatu.</b> Gunetik irteten da. Zer esan duen (titulua, esteka eta testua) Log-ean geratzen da <b>Anonimoa</b>Ez izenik, ez profilik, ez estekarik, eta esteka bat testu arrunt gisa erakusten da. Edonork irakurri ahal izango du, hitz-iragazki beraren pean, eduki sentikorren eta haurren mailako arauen arabera, edozein kideren hitzak bezala. Horrela jarraitzen du gunearen erregistroak: Wikipediak bezala, ekarpen guztiak gelditzen dira."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Deleted</b>: what members deleted, as Anonymous (below)."
msgstr "<b>Ezabatuta</b>: ezabatutako kideak, anonimo gisa (behean)."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Edits</b>: what members edited: who (Anonymous for an anonymous post or comment), when and the note they gave. A run of edits to one item is one line; the versions themselves are on the item's own history page. An edit in the first five minutes after something was written is part of writing it and isn't recorded, and an account can edit 30 times an hour."
msgstr "<b>Editatu</b>: zer editatu duten: nork (posta edo iruzkin anonimo baten izena), noiz eta oharra eman duten. Elementu baten edizio-zerrenda lerro bat da; bertsioak berak elementuaren historiaren orrian daude. Zerbait idatzi eta lehen bost minutuetako edizio bat idatzi eta grabatu gabe dago, eta kontu batek 30 aldiz edita dezake ordubetean."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Exiling or muting \"Anonymous #3\".</b> A guild's guildmasters can exile an anonymous person from the guild, or mute them in its channels, by their number. The guildmaster is never told whose it is: the site applies it to the account behind the number, and the guild's lists, its mod log and the Log show only \"Anonymous #3\". The person it was done to is told, can open the Log entry and can appeal it. A guildmaster who already suspects a particular account can still test that guess, so this keeps who it is from casual view, not from a determined guildmaster."
msgstr "<b>\"Anonymous\" #3\".</b> Guild baten moderatzaileek pertsona anonimo bat erbestera dezakete txiliotik, edo bere kanaletan mututu, zenbakiaren arabera. Moderatzailea ez da inoiz esaten norena den: webgunea zenbakiaren atzeko kontuari aplikatzen zaio, eta guild-en zerrendak, moderazio-erregistroa eta Log-a soilik \"Anonymous\" #3\". Esandako pertsonak egunkaria ireki dezake eta apela dezake. Kontu jakin bat susmatzen duen moderatzaileak oraindik ere proba dezake asmaketa hori, beraz, honek ez du uzten nor den ausazko ikuspegitik, ez moderatzaile zehatz batetik."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Guild changes</b>: what a guild's guildmasters changed in how it is run."
msgstr "<b>Guilden aldaketak</b>Hau da, guild-en moderatzaileak aldatu egin dira nola exekutatzen den."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Many at once.</b> In History > Manage you can tick up to 100 of your posts and comments and remove your name from them, or delete them, in one go. It asks for your password (and your two-factor code if you have one), and does exactly what the dialog does for each one: what can't be changed, such as a post for a Circle, is listed afterwards with the reason. History > Anonymous > Deleted lists what you deleted yourself, from the copies kept for you."
msgstr "<b>Asko batera.</b> Historian Kudeatu zure mezu eta iruzkinetako 100 arte, eta zure izena kendu edo ezabatu, joan batean. Pasahitza eskatzen du (eta bi faktoreko kodea, bat baldin baduzu), eta elkarrizketa-koadroak bakoitzari egiten diona egiten du: ezin da aldatu, Zirkulu baten mezua bezala, ondoren azaltzen da arrazoia. Historia > Anonimoa > Ezabatutako zerrendak ezabatu zenituen, zuretzat gordetako kopietatik."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Moderation</b>: a post or comment hidden or removed, restored, or hidden in a version. For each one: who (a guildmaster by name; the site's admins as \"Site admin\", never by name), when, where, which rule, and the reason written for it. It never shows the title or the text of what was hidden."
msgstr "<b>Moderazioa</b>: mezu edo iruzkin bat ezkutatua edo ezabatua, berrezarria edo ezkutatua bertsio batean. Bakoitzarentzat: nork (izenez moderatzailea; gunearen kudeatzaileak \"Administrazioa\", inoiz ez izenez), noiz, non, nork agintzen duen, eta zergatik idazten duen. Ez du inoiz erakusten ezkutatzen zenaren titulua edo testua."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Posts written with others.</b> Each author's credit can be anonymous on its own: when the post is anonymous from the start, when an author chooses \"Remove my name\" for their credit, or when they delete their account. Only that credit becomes \"Anonymous #N\"; the other authors stay named. Admins can always see whose it is."
msgstr "<b>Besteekin idatzitako mezuak.</b> Egile bakoitzaren kreditua anonimoa izan daiteke: mezua anonimoa denean hasieratik, autore batek \"Kendu nire izena\" aukeratzen duenean, edo kontua ezabatzen duenean. Kreditu hori bakarrik bihurtzen da \"Anonymous #N\"Beste autoreak izendatuta daude. Adminek beti ikus dezakete norena den."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Remove my name.</b> The post or comment stays where it is, with your name taken off, and leaves your profile. It can't be undone, and it isn't offered for a post made for a Circle, a post that has been tipped, or a post written with others."
msgstr "<b>Kendu nire izena.</b> Posta edo iruzkina non dagoen, zure izena kendu eta zure profila uzten du. Ezin da desegin, eta ez da eskaintzen Zirkulurako egindako post bat, posta bat, edo beste batzuekin idatzitakoa."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>Sanctions</b>: exiles, chat mutes, suspensions and bans, with the rule and the reason."
msgstr "<b>Zigorrak</b>Erbesteratuak, berriketa mutuak, esekidurak eta debekuak, araua eta arrazoia."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>The first five minutes.</b> If you delete something less than five minutes after you made it, and nobody else has commented on it, it is really erased: nothing is published and nothing is in the Log. The site keeps a private copy for 90 days, which only you and the site's admins can open. This is for a typo, a wrong picture or a post made in anger. It can be used 20 times a day; after that, and after five minutes, a delete is published as above."
msgstr "<b>Lehen bost minutuak.</b> Egin eta bost minutu baino gutxiagora zerbait ezabatzen baduzu, eta beste inork ez badu iruzkinik egin, ezabatu egiten da: ez da ezer argitaratzen eta ez dago ezer Egunkarian. Guneak 90 egunez kopia pribatu bat gordetzen du, zuk eta guneko administratzaileek bakarrik ireki dezaketena. Hau tipokeria, irudi okerra edo haserre egindako mezu bat da. Egunean 20 aldiz erabil daiteke; ondoren, eta bost minuturen buruan, ezabatua goian bezala argitaratzen da."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>What is never published:</b> the words of an item a moderator had removed or a guild had hidden, of an item in a banned guild, and of anything deleted by an account locked as a child's: those show a line and no words. A post made for a Circle, or in a private guild, is kept for that audience only."
msgstr "<b>Inoiz argitaratu ez dena:</b> Moderatzaile batek kendutako edo guild batek ezkutaturiko elementu baten hitzak, gai debekatu bateko elementuak, eta ume baten kontu batek ezabatutako edozer: lerro bat eta hitzik ez. Zirkulu baterako edo guild pribatu batean egindako mezua publiko horrentzat bakarrik gordetzen da."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "<b>When you delete your account.</b> Everything you wrote becomes Anonymous and stays on the site, where it was, instead of showing a deleted account. Nothing is removed, and it can't be undone. The one exception is an account less than 12 hours old, whose posts and comments are taken down as possible spam. Your private copies of what you erased yourself are emptied."
msgstr "<b>Zure kontua ezabatzen duzunean.</b> Idatzi duzun guztia anonimo bihurtzen da eta gunean geratzen da, non zegoen, ezabatutako kontu bat erakutsi ordez. Ez da ezer kentzen, eta ezin da desegin. Salbuespen bakarra 12 ordu baino gutxiagoko kontua da, eta mezuak eta iruzkinak ahalik eta baztergarrienak dira. Ezabatu duzunaren kopia pribatuak hustu egiten dira."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "<code>\"black cat\"</code>: posts with those words together, in that order."
msgstr "<code>\"black cat\"</code>: hitz horiekin batera, ordena horretan."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "<code>#gaming</code>: a topic, one of the site's categories or subcategories (Arts, Gaming, News, Film &amp; TV: letters and numbers only, so <code>#filmtv</code>). Search <code>#gam</code> to find the guilds in the topics with that in their name; <code>%(in_topic)s</code> narrows a post search to them."
msgstr "<code>#gaming</code>: gai bat, guneko kategoria edo azpikategoria bat (Arts, Gaming, News, Film) &amp; Telebista: letrak eta zenbakiak bakarrik. <code>#filmtv</code>). Bilatu <code>#gam</code> haien izenean gai horiei buruzko argibideak aurkitzea; <code>%(in_topic)s</code> bilaketa bat estutzen die."

#. each example is a search as it is typed: it stays as it is
#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "<code>%(example)s</code>: Alice's polls."
msgstr "<code>%(example)s</code>- Aliceren inkestak."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "<code>%(example)s</code>: links to example.com in +news this year."
msgstr "<code>%(example)s</code>: example.com webgunerako estekak +news Aurten."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "<code>%(example)s</code>: recipes in Spanish, each post once."
msgstr "<code>%(example)s</code>Errezetak gaztelaniaz, post bakoitza behin."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "<code>%(example)s</code>: videos in any guild about gaming."
msgstr "<code>%(example)s</code>-Jolasari buruzko bideoak."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "<code>%(example)s</code>: well-discussed posts about open source."
msgstr "<code>%(example)s</code>: iturburu irekiari buruzko mezu ongi sakabanatuak."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "<code>%(from_op)s</code> never finds an account's anonymous posts, and <code>%(not_from)s</code> never hides them. Nobody can find out who wrote an anonymous post by searching."
msgstr "<code>%(from_op)s</code> ez du inoiz kontu baten mezu anonimorik aurkitzen, eta <code>%(not_from)s</code> Ez ditu inoiz ezkutatzen. Inork ezin du jakin nork idatzi zuen mezu anonimo bat bilaketa bidez."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "<code>+pets</code>: a guild. Search <code>+pets</code> to find guilds with that in their name."
msgstr "<code>+pets</code>-Gild bat. Bilatu <code>+pets</code> haien izenean hori duten guildak aurkitzeko."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "<code>-%(key)s:</code> leaves them out"
msgstr "<code>-%(key)s:</code> Utz itzazu kanpoan"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "<code>-dogs</code> or <code>-\"hot dogs\"</code>: leaves out posts with that word or those words."
msgstr "<code>-dogs</code> edo <code>-\"hot dogs\"</code>: hitz edo hitz horiekin uzten ditu mezuak."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "<code>@alice</code>: an account. Search <code>@alice</code> to find accounts."
msgstr "<code>@alice</code>Kontu bat. Bilatu <code>@alice</code> kontuak bilatzeko."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "<code>black cat</code>: posts with both words, anywhere in the title or the text."
msgstr "<code>black cat</code>: bi hitz dituzten mezuak, tituluan edo testuan."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "<strong>GIFs and photos:</strong> GIPHY, Tenor and Flickr."
msgstr "<strong>GIFs eta argazkiak:</strong> GIPHY, Tenor eta Flickr."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "<strong>Music and podcasts:</strong> Spotify, SoundCloud, Apple Music, Apple Podcasts, Bandcamp, Mixcloud and Deezer show their player; nothing plays until you press it."
msgstr "<strong>Musika eta podcastak:</strong> Spotify, SoundCloudApple Music, Apple Podcasts, Bandcamp, Mixcloud eta Deezer-ek jokalaria erakusten dute; ezer ez da jolasten sakatu arte."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "<strong>Posts</strong> on X, Bluesky, Mastodon, Threads, Instagram, Reddit, Tumblr, Pinterest, Telegram and Truth Social show as a card with who wrote it and what they wrote. A Facebook post shows the page it is from; its text stays on Facebook."
msgstr "<strong>Mezuak</strong> X-en, Bluesky, MastodonHariak, Instagram, Reddit, Tumblr, Pinterest, Telegram eta Truth Social Erakutsi txartel gisa nork idatzi duen eta zer idatzi duen. A Facebook Post-ek erakusten du nondik datorren orria; bere testua hemen dago Facebook."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "<strong>Videos play in the post:</strong> YouTube, Vimeo, Dailymotion, Twitch, Kick, Rumble, Odysee, BitChute, Bilibili, Streamable, Loom and TED; Facebook videos and reels, Instagram reels and TikTok videos play when you press play."
msgstr "<strong>Bideoak postan daude:</strong> YouTubeVimeo, Dailymotion, Twitch, Kick, Rumble, Odysee, BitChute, Bilibili, Streamable, Loom eta TED; Facebook bideoak eta zintak, Instagram bobinak eta TikTok Bideoak erreproduzitzen ari dira erreproduzitzen duzunean."

msgid "A **bot** is an account that posts by itself. The site's admins approve every one before it posts anything, and every bot follows the same posting rules, and the [rules for bots](/help/rules#bots) in the Rules and Guidelines."
msgstr ""

#, machine, plain1
msgid "A **member bot** needs its member to run it: a script of their own with a **bot key** (for example for X), or a source they pay for. It stays the member's, they manage it, and its profile says **Automated by @member**. A member bot may read approved feeds too."
msgstr "**member bot** batek bere kidea behar du exekutatzeko: beren script bat **bot gakoarekin** (X, adibidez), edo ordaintzen duten iturburu bat. Kidearena izaten jarraitzen du, kudeatzen dute, eta bere profilaren arabera, ** @member**-k automatikoa. Bot batek onartutako iturriak ere irakur ditzake."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "A **site bot** costs nothing to run: it reads free feeds (below). Anyone can propose one, and once an admin approves it, it is the **site's**: the admins run it, it is linked to nobody, and its profile says **Automated by %(site)s**. A BBC headlines bot is a site bot."
msgstr "Bot-ak ez du ezertarako balio: iturri libreak irakurtzen ditu (behean). Edonork proposa dezake bat, eta behin administratzaile batek onartu ondoren, **site's** da: administratzaileek exekutatu egiten dute, ez zaio inori estekatzen, eta bere profilek dio **Automatikoki %(site)s**-k. BBCko titularraren bot bat guneko bot bat da."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "A JSON object with the posts, best first, and optionally a cursor to ask for more:"
msgstr "Postudun JSON objektua, lehen onena eta aukerako kurtsorea, gehiago eskatzeko:"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "A bot that breaks the site's rules is paused or banned like any account, and so is the member running it when the bot was the point."
msgstr "Gunearen arauak hausten dituen bot bat isildu egiten da edo debekatu egiten da, edozein kontu bezala, eta bot-a zen momentuan exekutatzen da."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "A bot that needs a key or a paid source is a member bot; one that only reads free feeds can be a site bot."
msgstr "Gako bat edo iturburu ordaindu bat behar duen bot bat bot kide bat da; iturri libreak soilik irakurtzen dituenak bot bat izan daiteke."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "A bot's posts are on its own profile, like everyone's. It can forward them to up to %(num)s guilds, and each guild's own rules apply: a guild can refuse forwards from bots, and one that only takes forwards from approved contributors needs the bot to be one. When a guild refuses, the post stays on the bot's profile."
msgid_plural "A bot's posts are on its own profile, like everyone's. It can forward them to up to %(num)s guilds, and each guild's own rules apply: a guild can refuse forwards from bots, and one that only takes forwards from approved contributors needs the bot to be one. When a guild refuses, the post stays on the bot's profile."
msgstr[0] "Bot baten mezuak bere profilean daude, guztionak bezala. %(num)s guilderaino eraman ditzake, eta bakoitzak bere arauak aplikatzen ditu: ontzi batek botei uko egin diezaieke, eta laguntzaile homologatuei bakarrik aurre egiten dienak bot bat izan behar du. Gild batek ezetz esaten duenean, posta bot-aren profilean geratuko da."
msgstr[1] "Bot baten mezuak bere profilean daude, guztionak bezala. %(num)s guilderaino hel daitezke, eta guild bakoitzak bere arauak aplikatzen ditu: ontzi batek botetatik atzera egin dezake, eta laguntzaile homologatuetatik aurrera doan batek bot bat behar du. Gild batek ezetz esaten duenean, posta bot-aren profilean geratuko da."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "A comment search needs a word of at least 3 letters, or <code>%(from_op)s</code> or <code>%(in_op)s</code>."
msgstr "Iruzkin baten bilaketak gutxienez hiru letrako hitza behar du, edo <code>%(from_op)s</code> edo <code>%(in_op)s</code>."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "A complete example"
msgstr "Adibide osoa"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "A curation normally picks and orders its posts with rules its owner sets on the site. Instead, a curation can name a **feed server**: a small web service that you (or someone you trust) run, which answers with the posts to show and the order to show them in. How your server decides is up to you."
msgstr "Iturri zaindu batek normalean bere postuak hautatzen eta ordenatzen ditu bere jabearen arauekin. Horren ordez, janari zaindu batek **feed zerbitzari** izena eman dezake: zuk (edo zure konfiantzazko norbaitek) exekutatzen duzun web-zerbitzu txiki bat, eta horrek mezuekin erantzuten du erakusteko eta erakusteko ordenarekin. Zerbitzariak nola erabakitzen duen zure esku dago."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "A failure by %(site)s in one or more instances to insist upon your strict adherence to these licence terms, shall not be construed as a waiver of any continuing or subsequent violations of these license terms."
msgstr "%(site)s(e)k huts egin du lizentzia-baldintza hauei zure atxikimendu zorrotza gogorarazteko kasu batean edo gehiagotan, ez da lizentzia-baldintza hauen etengabeko edo ondorengo urraketarik onartuko."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "A feed a member adds to a running bot waits for an admin. Removing one takes effect at once."
msgstr "Kide batek exekutatzen ari den bot bati gehitzen dion iturria administratzailearen zain dago. Bat kentzeak berehala eragiten du."

#. floor and quiet are minutes (the shortest and the longest wait between two
#. reads of a feed), per_run is a number of items, daily a number of posts
#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "A feed is read as often as it safely can be: every %(floor)s minutes at most, or less often if the feed asks to be (most news feeds say 15 minutes), and less often again while it has nothing new (up to every %(quiet)s minutes). A feed that asks us to slow down is left alone for as long as it says. New items are posted oldest first, at most %(per_run)s from one feed at a time and %(daily)s a day for the whole bot."
msgstr "Iturri bat ahalik eta gehien irakurtzen da: %(floor)s minutu oro gehienez, edo gutxiagotan, iturriak hala eskatzen badu (albiste gehienek 15 minutu esaten dute), eta gutxiagotan, ezer berririk ez duen bitartean (%(quiet)s minutu bakoitzeko). Moteltzeko eskatzen digun iturria bakarrik geratzen da esaten duen bitartean. Elementu berriak lehenago argitaratzen dira, gehienez ere %(per_run)s iturri batetik aldi berean eta %(daily)s egun batetik bot osoarentzat."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "A feed that keeps failing (%(num)s times in a row) stops and the member running it is told; start it again from Settings > Bots once it works."
msgid_plural "A feed that keeps failing (%(num)s times in a row) stops and the member running it is told; start it again from Settings > Bots once it works."
msgstr[0] "Huts egiten jarraitzen duen iturria (%(num)s aldiz jarraian) gelditzen da eta exekutatzen ari denari esaten zaio; hasi berriro Ezarpenak >tik. Bot-ak behin funtzionatzen duenean."
msgstr[1] "Huts egiten jarraitzen duen iturria (%(num)s aldiz jarraian) gelditzen da eta exekutatzen ari denari esaten zaio; hasi berriro Ezarpenak >-etik. Bot-ak behin funtzionatzen duenean."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "A member bot can also post from a script of its member's own, through a **bot key**. This is how to run a bot for **X**: X has no feeds, and its terms don't allow other sites to scrape it, so use your own X access in your own script and post each tweet's link. The site shows a link to a tweet as X's own embed, so no tweet text is copied. Site bots have no keys."
msgstr "Bot kide batek bere kidearen script batetik ere idatz dezake, **bot gakoa** baten bidez. Hau bot bat exekutatzeko modua da **X**: X-k ez du iturririk, eta bere terminoek ez dute uzten beste guneek hura ezaba dezaten, beraz, erabili zure X sarbidea zure scriptean eta bidali txio bakoitzaren esteka. Webguneak esteka bat erakusten du txio bati X-ren kapsula gisa, beraz ez da tuit-testurik kopiatuko. Guneko botek ez dute teklarik."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "A post always belongs to its author's profile first. Anyone can \"Forward\" it into other Guilds for community-scoped discussion - each Guild a post is forwarded to gets its own independent copy, with its own votes and its own comments. Users can add comments to posts or to other comments."
msgstr "Postu bat beti egilearen profilarena da lehenik. Edonork sar dezake beste Guild batzuetan, eztabaida komunitariorako - Guild bakoitzak mezu bat bidaltzen du bere kopia independentea lortzeko, bere botoekin eta bere iruzkinekin. Erabiltzaileek iruzkinak gehi ditzakete mezuei edo beste iruzkin batzuei."

#, machine, plain2
msgid "A private guild's decisions are read only by its own members and the site's admins, and the guild is never named in the public Log. What the site does to run itself (its defences, its lists, its bots) is read by the admins only. The site's automatic checks write generic lines: \"Automatic spam check\", \"Automatic image check\"."
msgstr "Guild-en erabaki pribatuak bere kideek eta gunearen administratzaileek bakarrik irakurtzen dituzte, eta gremioa ez da egunkari publikoan izendatzen. Guneak egiten duena (bere defentsak, zerrendak, bot-ak) administratzaileek bakarrik irakurtzen dute. Gunearen kontrol automatikoek lerro orokorrak idazten dituzte: \"Automatikoki spam-kontrola\", \"Irudi-kontrol automatikoa\"."

#. parts is the most words and operators a search can hold, chars the most
#. characters
#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "A search can hold up to %(parts)s words and operators, and up to %(chars)s characters."
msgstr "Bilaketa batek %(parts)s hitz eta eragileraino eta %(chars)s karaktereraino iraun dezake."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "A search only finds what you could see anyway: your word filter, blocks, mutes and private guilds all still apply. A search for one account (<code>%(from_op)s</code>) shows their posts even if you muted them."
msgstr "Bilaketa batek, hala ere, ikusi dezakezuna bakarrik aurkitzen du: zure hitz-iragazkia, blokeak, mutuak eta guild pribatuak. Kontu bat bilatzeko (<code>%(from_op)s</code>) beren mezuak erakusten ditu mututu badituzu ere."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "A successful refresh will result in the following response:"
msgstr "Freskagarri arrakastatsu batek honako erantzuna emango du:"

#, glossary, machine, plain2
msgid "About"
msgstr "Guri buruz"

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "About - %(site)s"
msgstr "Honi buruz - %(site)s"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Access tokens expire one hour after they are issued. To maintain ongoing access, you will need to use the refresh token to obtain a new access token."
msgstr "Sarbide-tokenak bidali eta ordubetera iraungitzen dira. Etengabeko sarbidea mantentzeko, token freskagarria erabili beharko duzu sarbide-token berria lortzeko."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Accounts that post by themselves, approved by the site's admins."
msgstr "Posta-kontuak, webgunearen administratzaileek onartutakoak."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Additionally, no current Guildmaster (or no Guildmaster above you, if you are a Guildmaster already) may have done any of the following in the past 60 days:"
msgstr "Gainera, ez dago Guildeko moderatzailerik (edo zure gaineko Guild moderatzailerik, dagoeneko Guild moderatzailea bazara) azken 60 egunetan honelakorik egin duenik:"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Additionally, other countries such as Germany, the United Kingdom, and China have legal prohibitions on speech that the government deems to be \"offensive\". These laws violate their citizens' human rights to free speech. Platforms with assets, personnel, or data in these countries must comply with those anti-free-speech laws or face consequences."
msgstr "Gainera, Alemania, Erresuma Batua eta Txina bezalako beste herrialde batzuek legezko debekuak dituzte gobernuak \"ondasun\"tzat jotzen dituen hitzaldietan. Lege horiek herritarren giza eskubideak urratzen dituzte adierazpen askerako. Herrialde horietako ondasun, langile edo datudun plataformek adierazpen-kontrako lege horiek bete behar dituzte edo ondorioei aurre egin."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Additionally, there are legal restrictions on certain specific types of speech. Examples of these restrictions include (but are not limited to):"
msgstr "Gainera, lege-murrizketak daude zenbait hizketa-motatan. Mugaketa hauen adibideak daude (baina ez daude mugatuta):"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Advocacy of imminent lawless behavior"
msgstr "Legerik gabeko portaera berehalakoa"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Alignment"
msgstr "Lerrokatzea"

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Already using %(site)s? <a href=\"%(url)s\">Sign in</a>"
msgstr "Dagoeneko erabilita %(site)s? <a href=\"%(url)s\">Hasi saioa</a>"

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Alter posts, comments, username identification, or any other content found on %(site)s."
msgstr "Postu aldaketak, iruzkinak, erabiltzaile-izenaren identifikazioa edo %(site)s(e)n aurkitutako beste edozein eduki."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "An account, guild, topic or curation you can't see reads as one that does not exist."
msgstr "Kontu bat, koipetsua, gaia edo janari zaindua, ez da existitzen."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Anonymous comments are never found with <code>%(from_op)s</code>."
msgstr "Iruzkin anonimoak ez dira inoiz aurkitu <code>%(from_op)s</code>."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Any file provided by %(company)s in response to a legal process, such as a search warrant, will be accompanied by a cryptographic signature. A file may be submitted here, with its signature. If this page does not validate the signature, then the file may not be authentic, and you should suspect tampering or mishandling."
msgstr "Prozesu judizial bati erantzuteko %(company)sk emandako edozein fitxategi, hala nola bilaketa-agindua, sinadura kriptografiko batekin batera egongo da. Fitxategi bat aurkez daiteke hemen, bere sinadurarekin. Orrialde honek sinadura balioztatzen ez badu, agian fitxategia ez da benetakoa izango, eta susmoa hartu beharko zenuke iruzur egiten edo gaizki kudeatzen ari zarela."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Any text, lists or quotes"
msgstr "Edozein testu, zerrenda edo komatxo"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Applications"
msgstr "Aplikazioak"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Article guide:"
msgstr "Artikuluaren gida:"

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "As an example, you can test this page using the %(site)s logo <a href=\"%(url)s\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Its signature is <code>%(signature)s</code>."
msgstr "Adibide gisa, orrialde hau proba dezakezu. %(site)s logotipoa <a href=\"%(url)s\" target=\"_blank\">hemen</a>Bere sinadura da <code>%(signature)s</code>."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "As discussed above, threats and intimidation are explicitly *not* protected speech. If you are signed in to %(site)s, you will be able to use the built-in Flag option to bring threats (or other malicious content) to the attention of the %(site)s administrators."
msgstr "Lehen aipatu bezala, mehatxuak eta intimidazioa esplizituki dira *ez * babestutako hitzaldia. %(site)s(r)ekin sinatua bazaude, bandera integratua aukera erabil dezakezu %(site)s administratzaileei mehatxuak (edo bestelako eduki gaiztoak) ekartzeko."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "As specifically permitted by a separate written agreement you have with %(company)s"
msgstr "%(company)s(r)ekin duzun hitzarmen idatziak baimentzen duen bezala"

#, machine, plain2
msgid "Asking for words to come down"
msgstr "Hitzak jaisteko eskatzen"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Automated posts are public link posts: never anonymous, for circles or co-authored. They can be forwarded to guilds you choose, under each guild's rules."
msgstr "Postu automatizatuak esteka publikoak dira: inoiz ez anonimoak, zirkuluak edo egilekideak. Zuk aukeratzen dituzun koipeak ekar diezazkieke, guild bakoitzaren arauen arabera."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Awesome online communities, without censorship"
msgstr "Interneteko komunitate zoragarriak, zentsurarik gabe"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Badges are sorted into bronze, silver, gold, and diamond tiers, based on the relative difficulty of obtaining them."
msgstr "Badeak brontzezko, zilarrezko, urrezko eta diamantezko lauzetan sailkatzen dira, lortzeko zailtasun erlatiboan oinarrituta."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Block formatting"
msgstr "Blokeen formatua"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Blockquote"
msgstr "Aipu blokea"

#, machine, plain1
msgctxt "formatting"
msgid "Bold"
msgstr "Lodia"

#, glossary, machine, plain2
msgid "Bots"
msgstr "Botak"

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Bots - %(site)s"
msgstr "Bots - %(site)s"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Bots post and forward. They never comment, vote, chat or lead a guild, and nobody can sign in as one. A bot's posts can take tips: a member bot's go to its member. Every bot's profile says who runs it (the site, or @member), and every bot post carries the robot mark. If you'd rather not see bots, turn on **Hide bot content** in **Settings > Content**."
msgstr "Bots posta eta aurrera. Ez dute inoiz iruzkinik egiten, bozkatzen, berriketan edo txilio bat gidatzen, eta inork ezin du bat bezala sinatu. Bot baten mezuek aholkuak har ditzakete: bot kide bat kidearengana doa. bot bakoitzaren profilak dio nork exekutatzen duen (webgunea, edo @member), eta bot bakoitzak robotaren marka darama. Nahiago baduzu bot-ak ez ikusi, piztu **Ezkutatu bot-aren edukia** barruan **Ezarpenak > Edukia**."

#, machine, plain1
msgctxt "formatting"
msgid "Button"
msgstr "Botoia"

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Capitalize \"%(company)s\""
msgstr "Kapitalizatu \"%(company)s\""

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Capitalize \"%(site)s\", except when using it as part of \"ruqqus.com\" or within links"
msgstr "\"%(site)s\" maiuskulaz jarri, \"ruqqus.com\" edo \"esteka\" gisa erabiltzen denean izan ezik"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Capitalize \"ruqqus.com\""
msgstr "Capitalize \"ruqqus.com\""

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Chat Help"
msgstr "Berriketa-zerbitzua"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "China's entire internet infrastructure sits behind a massive government firewall, allowing the Chinese government to monitor and block anything they like from outside the country. (commonly referred to as \"the Great Firewall of China.\")"
msgstr "Txinako Interneteko azpiegitura osoa gobernuaren suebaki masibo baten atzean dago, Txinako gobernuak nahi duen guztia kontrolatu eta blokeatu ahal izateko. (Batez ere \"Txinako suebaki Handia\" deitzen zaio)"

#, glossary, machine, plain2
msgid "Close"
msgstr "Itxi"

#, machine, plain1
msgctxt "formatting"
msgid "Code"
msgstr "Kodea"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Code Block"
msgstr "Kode blokea"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Coloring"
msgstr "Koloreztatzea"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Colour, highlight, alignment and buttons"
msgstr "Kolorea, nabarmentzea, lerrokatzea eta botoiak"

#, glossary, machine, plain2
msgctxt "noun"
msgid "Comment"
msgstr "Iruzkina"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Comment on other people's posts and engage in boundless, free discussion without censorship."
msgstr "Besteen mezuei buruz hitz egin eta eztabaida mugagabean jardun zentsurarik gabe."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Comments follow the same rules as everywhere else: your word filter, the accounts you blocked or muted, and private guilds and Circle posts you can't open are never shown. Comments under a post you can't open are left out, so a page can have fewer than 25 results."
msgstr "Iragazki hitza, blokeatu edo mututu dituzun kontuak, eta ireki ezin dituzun hutsune pribatuak ez dira inoiz erakusten. Ireki ezin diren mezuetako iruzkinak kanpoan geratzen dira, beraz, orri batek 25 emaitza baino gutxiago izan ditzake."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Comments: <code>%(example)s</code>, or <code>%(other)s</code>."
msgstr "Iruzkinak: <code>%(example)s</code>edo <code>%(other)s</code>."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Congress shall make no law respecting an establishment of religion, or prohibiting the free exercise thereof; or abridging the freedom of speech, or of the press; or the right of the people peaceably to assemble, and to petition the Government for a redress of grievances."
msgstr "Kongresuak ez du inolako legerik egingo erlijio-egoera bati buruz, ezta horren ariketa askea debekatu ere, ezta adierazpen-askatasuna edo prentsa-askatasuna zabaldu ere, edo herriak bakean biltzeko eta gobernuari kexak zuzentzeko eskatzeko duen eskubidea ere."

#, glossary, machine, plain2
msgid "Connect"
msgstr "Sare sozialak"

#, glossary, machine, plain2
msgid "Contact"
msgstr "Harremanetarako"

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Contact %(company)s"
msgstr "Kontaktua %(company)s"

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Contact %(site)s"
msgstr "Kontaktua %(site)s"

#, machine, plain1
msgctxt "noun: what people post on the site"
msgid "Content"
msgstr "Edukia"

#, glossary, machine, plain2
msgid "Contribute"
msgstr "Lagundu"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Copyright"
msgstr "Copyright-a"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Copyrighted works may not be distributed without the permission of the copyright owner."
msgstr "Copyrightdun lanak ezin dira copyrightaren jabearen baimenik gabe banatu."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Courts may issue a non-disclosure order (\"gag order\") to participants in a legal proceeding, preventing the participants from discussing the proceeding publicly."
msgstr "Epaitegiek ezeztapen-agindu bat eman diezaiekete parte-hartzaileei lege-prozedura batean, parte-hartzaileei prozesua publikoki eztabaida ez dezaten."

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Create a %(site)s account in seconds and join your favorite communities. Usernames aplenty. No email required."
msgstr "Sortu %(site)s kontua segundotan eta sartu zure gogoko komunitateetan. Erabiltzaile-izenak asko dira. Ez da postarik behar."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Create a comment in the guild being sieged"
msgstr "Sortu iruzkin bat guild-en setiatzean"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Crypto address copied to clipboard"
msgstr "Crypto helbidea arbelean kopiatuta"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Curation Mention"
msgstr "Curated feed Mention"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Custom Formatting"
msgstr "Formatu pertsonalizatua"

#, machine, plain1
msgid "DO NOT reveal your Client Secret. Anyone with your Client Secret will be able to pretend to be you. You are responsible for keeping your Client Secret a secret!"
msgstr "Ez erakutsi zure bezeroaren sekretua. Zure bezero-sekretua duen edonork zu zarela esan dezake. Zure bezero sekretua gordetzeko ardura duzu!"

#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "Days are in UTC. <code>%(before)s</code> and <code>%(after)s</code> leave the day itself out; <code>%(since)s</code> and <code>%(until)s</code> include it."
msgstr "Egunak sartzen dira UTC. <code>%(before)s</code> eta <code>%(after)s</code> Utz ezazu eguna bera; <code>%(since)s</code> eta <code>%(until)s</code> Sartu."

#, machine, plain1
msgid "Defamation (Negative and harmful remarks about someone else which the speaker knows to be factually untrue)"
msgstr "Defamazioa (hitz egiten duen beste bati buruzko ohar negatiboak eta kaltegarriak egia esan ez dela dakiena)"

#, machine, plain2
msgid "Deleting a post or comment has two ways, and you choose in the dialog:"
msgstr "Mezu edo iruzkin bat ezabatzeak bi bide ditu, eta elkarrizketa-koadroan aukeratu:"

